/// MISCOMPILE — SILENT WRONG VALUE (2026-07-14, seed rcdzc, iter 42). The MUTUAL-RECURSION face of the
/// still-live-binding family. A function `fc` that matches a node binding its child list `elems`, then in
/// ONE operand reads the whole `node` again (here via `head-of(node)`) while a SIBLING operand passes
/// `elems` to a list-walker `fl` that RECURSES BACK INTO `fc` — the mutual `fc ↔ fl` walk consumes
/// `elems` (which ALIASES `node`'s heap payload), corrupting the sibling `head-of(node)` read.
/// `cdz check` CLEAN; `cdz compile` SUCCEEDS; runs WRONG.
///
/// ⚠ STILL OPEN after the still-live-binding RETAIN fix (spec@6c1120b2, 2026-07-15) that closed the
/// Param/LocalRef faces (`…-consuming-op-mutates-still-live-binding`, `…-selfcall-plus-consuming-op-…`,
/// `…-concat-consumes-still-live-lhs-…`). This face is DISTINCT: the value consumed is a `sum-payload(node)`
/// PAYLOAD binder (`elems`), a BORROW that shares `node`'s single refcount — not a `Param`/`LocalRef` the
/// RETAIN analysis tracks. SHARPENED BISECTION (2026-07-15, all `cdz compile`+`cdz-run`):
///   • Threshold is the SUM's VARIANT COUNT, not the tree/recursion. `Ast` with 5 variants (Int/Str/Bool/
///     Name/List) → WRONG (returns 1); the IDENTICAL program with a 2-variant `Ast` (Name/List only) →
///     CORRECT (101/102). So the multi-variant sum-match dispatch (br_table/if-chain over ≥3 variants)
///     mishandles the payload's lifetime; the 2-variant if-dispatch does not.
///   • The sibling read must read node's PAYLOAD, not just its DISCRIMINANT: `head-of(node)` (reads
///     `sum-payload(node)` = the array `elems` aliases) → WRONG; `is-list(node)` (only `sum-disc(node)`,
///     no payload read) alongside the same `fl(elems)` → CORRECT (101). So it is the PAYLOAD-array
///     alias (node's payload == elems) being consumed by `fl` while `head-of` re-extracts it.
///   • Reading the head from `elems` DIRECTLY (`head-e(elems)`) instead of re-extracting via `node`
///     (`head-of(node)`) → CORRECT (101) — one path to the array, no alias to corrupt.
/// So the root: `elems = sum-payload(node)` is a borrowed alias of node's payload (no rc++); passing it to
/// the consuming mutual call `fl(elems)` while `node`'s payload is ALSO read (via `head-of(node)`) frees
/// the shared array. FIX DIRECTION: a `SumPayload` binder used in a CONSUMING position while its SCRUTINEE
/// is still live (read again in the same arm) must `dup` — the RETAIN analysis (`collect_dup_sites` in
/// backend/wasm/select.rs) currently only tracks `Param`/`LocalRef` binders, not `SumPayload` aliases, and
/// only within one function (this needs the aggregate/parent liveness, and the ≥3-variant dispatch path).
///
///   fc (List [Name "a", Int 5]):
///     match node { List(elems) => head-of(node) [Some→100 | None→0]  +  fl(elems) }
///   head-of(node) should be Some("a") → 100, and fl sums the child fc's = 1, so 101.
///   IT RETURNS 1  — head-of(node) reads None, because fl(elems)'s mutual recursion into fc consumed the
///   `elems` payload that `node` shares, so the sibling `head-of(node)` sees a corrupted node.
///
/// SHARP (each necessary — this is a NARROW combination):
///   • `fl` must RECURSE BACK INTO `fc` (mutual recursion). An INLINE list walk in the same arm that does
///     NOT call `fc` back is CORRECT (101) — so it is the `fc↔fl` mutual cycle consuming the shared payload,
///     not merely "walk elems".
///   • the sibling `head-of(node)` reads the WHOLE `node` (the aggregate whose payload `elems` is);
///     reading only `elems` (e.g. `List.len(elems)`) alongside the walk is fine.
///   • a `let`-bound `elems` + `head-of(node)` WITHOUT the mutual recursion is correct; a NON-recursive
///     helper is correct. Only the mutual `fc↔fl` cycle over the shared payload corrupts.
///
/// This is the same missing-dup root as the rest of the still-live-binding family
/// (`miscompile-consuming-op-mutates-still-live-binding`, `…-selfcall-plus-consuming-op-share-param`,
/// `…-env-interpreter-shadow-corrupts-outer-binding`): a value still read after its payload is consumed
/// needs a `dup`, and the mutual-recursion arg path omits it. IMPACT: this is the IDIOMATIC homoiconic-Ast
/// resolver shape — a `check(node)` / `check-list(elems)` mutual pair that both dispatches on the node's
/// HEAD and recurses into its children — so a scope-checker written the natural way over the canonical
/// `Ast` silently misreads every node whose head it inspects while recursing (see the withheld
/// `scopecheck` free-var counts). Fix locus: dup the aggregate operand of a mutual-recursive call whose
/// callee consumes the payload a sibling still reads (backend/wasm/select.rs, the mutual-call arg path).
type Ast =
  | Int(Int64)
  | Str(String)
  | Bool(Bool)
  | Name(String)
  | List(List(Ast))

def head-of(node: Ast) = match node with
  | Ast.List([Ast.Name(n), .. _]) => Some(n)
  | _ => None(unit)

def fc(node: Ast) = match node with
  | Ast.Name(_) => 1
  | Ast.List(elems) => (match head-of(node) with
      | Some(_) => 100
      | None(_) => 0) + fl(elems)
  | _ => 0

def fl(elems: List(Ast)) = match elems with
  | [] => 0
  | [h, .. r] => fc(h) + fl(r)

/// `fc (List [Name "a", Int 5])` — head-of=Some→100, fl=1 → should be 101; returns 1 (head reads None).
def run() = fc(Ast.List([Ast.Name("a"), Ast.Int(5)]))

export { run }
